  "body": "The Sodick wire post of issue 617 (`assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps`) refuses a 4-axis Wire Contour by name (\"is a 4-axis cut - ... no G74 / G75 or U V words\").\n\nWanted: the 4-axis cut (upper and lower profile, PARAM WireFourAxis, WireU / WireV) in Sodick's own words. The 1998 \"Wire EDM Machine Operation\" manual (Mark 21 / EX21) lists G74 / G75 (4-axis on / off) and U V (upper guide) but the pages read for issue 617 do not state whether U V are absolute upper-guide positions or offsets from X Y, nor the plane heights the control assumes. Those must be confirmed from a public Sodick source or by a machine owner before code.\n\nClean-room: public sources only; the sample program attached to issue 617 is another CAM's output and is not a source.\n\nDone means: a 4-axis punch posts through `sodick-wire.cps` to a new golden with each word named by its source, with the U V meaning stated in the decision file; or the refusal stays and the PR records what could not be confirmed.\n\nPart of #617\n",
